;;;; vp9/scans.lisp — GENERATED.  The coefficient scan orders, and the neighbours they imply.
;;;;
;;;; VP9 has three scans per transform size and picks between them by the INTRA PREDICTION MODE: a
;;;; vertically predicted block has residual that varies mostly horizontally, so it is scanned
;;;; column-wise, and vice versa.  That is unusual — every other codec here has one scan per
;;;; transform — and it is why the scan is selected per block rather than per picture.
;;;;
;;;; The NEIGHBOUR tables are derived here rather than transcribed.  A coefficient's context is how
;;;; many non-zero coefficients its already-scanned neighbours had, and which neighbours those are
;;;; follows from the scan: a column scan knows the sample to the left, a row scan the one above, and
;;;; the default scan both.  Deriving it and CHECKING the derivation against every one of ffmpeg's
;;;; twelve tables says something a transcription cannot — that the rule is the rule, and not twelve
;;;; coincidences.

(in-package #:reel.vp9)

